<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμοργός</span></b>  (A), ὁ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέργω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who squeezes</i> or <i>drains,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμοργοί, πόλεως ὄλεθροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					214
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέμων λαμπτῆρας ἀμοργούς</span>
			lanterns <i>which protect</i> [the light] <i>from</i> winds,
				F.m<i><span class="en">
				p.84
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> proparox.
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμοργος</span></b>  (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμεργος</span>
			), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμόργη</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				86.34
			</span></i>, al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
